EXAMPLE a TOOL prints the fields of its ToolSpec and the descriptions of its arguments
  SOURCE TOOL search_scene SCENE RO "Search."
  SOURCE   FLAG tier1
  SOURCE   TIMEOUT 15.0
  SOURCE   MAXCHARS 30000
  SOURCE   ARG query str "Syntax"
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 50
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'search_scene': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'category': 'SCENE',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'effect': 'RO',
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'tier1': True,
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'timeout_s': 15.0,
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'max_chars': 30000,
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec direct_only
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'query': "Syntax",
  EXPECT unrendered.pyparams limit

EXAMPLE a FORWARD tool prints its expectation and its wrapper, which leaves out an OMIT argument that equals its default
  SOURCE TOOL search_scene SCENE RO "Search."
  SOURCE   FORWARD
  SOURCE   DOC "root: scope \"here\"."
  SOURCE   DOC "limit: max."
  SOURCE   ARG query str
  SOURCE   ARG root ostr DEFAULT None
  SOURCE   ARG limit int DEFAULT 50 OMIT
  SOURCE   ARG count int DEFAULT 5
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('search_scene', 'RO', "Search.", (
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('root', ostr, None),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ('limit', int, 50),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools @tools.provide
  EXPECT rendered.pytools async def search_scene(
  EXPECT rendered.pytools root: ostr = None,
  EXPECT rendered.pytools ("Search."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    root: scope \"here\"."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools "\n    limit: max."
  EXPECT rendered.pytools query=rt.w_str(query),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools root=rt.w_ostr(root),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools limit=rt.w_int(limit, 50),
  EXPECT rendered.pytools count=rt.w_int(count),

EXAMPLE a PYTOOL is direct_only, escapes its descriptions, and prints only an expectation like a TOOL that is not FORWARD
  SOURCE PYTOOL use_skill SYSTEM RW "Use."
  SOURCE   ARG name str "say \"hi\" \\ bye"
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW "X."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'use_skill': {
  EXPECT rendered.pyspec 'direct_only': True,
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec tier1
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec timeout_s
  EXPECT unrendered.pyspec max_chars
  EXPECT rendered.pyparams 'name': "say \"hi\" \\ bye",
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('use_skill', 'RW', "Use.", (
  EXPECT rendered.pytools tools.expect('x', 'RW', "X.", (
  EXPECT unrendered.pytools async def

EXAMPLE a name or an argument twice
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RO "X."
  SOURCE   ARG a str
  SOURCE   ARG a int
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE RW "X."
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 3:7
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 5:6

EXAMPLE an effect, a category or a type outside the lists, no summary, OMIT without a default
  SOURCE TOOL x SCENE WRITE "X."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL y SCENES RO "Y."
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL z SCENE RO "Z."
  SOURCE   ARG a integer
  SOURCE   ARG b int OMIT
  SOURCE END
  SOURCE TOOL w SCENE RO
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:14
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:9
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:13
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 9:14

EXAMPLE a PYTOOL is direct_only already and has no Unity-side words: unity_transport, MAXCHARS
  SOURCE PYTOOL x SYSTEM RO "X."
  SOURCE   FLAG unity_transport
  SOURCE   FLAG direct_only
  SOURCE   MAXCHARS 5
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 4:3
